# Expo Router is a single-page app: every path must serve index.html, or deep
# links (e.g. /workspace) 404 on refresh or direct entry.
#
# This replaces the `routes: [{ type: rewrite, source: /*, destination:
# /index.html }]` block that did the same job in render.yaml. It lives in
# public/ because `expo export --platform web` copies that directory verbatim
# into dist/, and Cloudflare Pages reads _redirects from the root of what it
# serves.
#
# The 200 is load-bearing: without it this is a 302 to /index.html and the
# browser's address bar loses the route the user asked for.
#
# Keep the catch-all last. _redirects is applied top to bottom and stops at
# the first match, so any future rule placed below this one is dead.
/*    /index.html   200
